The M3b4 child has the decision and is resuming. Still running:
- the A11r1 cold leg on EC2;
- #9784 4b2 (615ad85a);
- the #9550 merge and full gate (dcc8896c);
- the `master` control for the one failing policy test.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- `.expect("model follows dispatch")` assumed that every `model(call)` follows a `dispatch(call)` on the same live memo. That only holds while the memo keeps every entry. Once a budget can refuse entries, the assumption becomes a panic, so a bounded memo forces the side channel to become an ordinary query.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

A11r1 is still in the cold leg. It started about 03:21Z after the roughly 5-minute build, and a cold leg took about 72 minutes last time, so I expect the end at around 04:35Z. The supervision watch has seen no terminal state.

Running now:
- #9784 4b2 (615ad85a);
- the #9550 full gate (dcc8896c);
- #9746 M3b4 (cd5cc494);
- the bisect that finds which #9746 commit broke `one_subset_run_makes_mixed_batch_unreliable`.

The bisect's first point passes: `master` `3d8424b51e`, the commit the lane merged, passes the test. So the regression comes from a #9746 lane commit, and the bisect is now testing those commits. A11r1 is still in its cold leg.

Running:
- validation of my dispatch-model refactor;
- the bisect;
- A11r1;
- #9784 4b2 (615ad85a);
- the #9550 gate (dcc8896c).

The #9550 audit child (adde40e0) is sorting the 17 failures into identity-only, completion-only and real differences. It re-blesses only the identity-only ones, after showing that their normalized diff is empty.

Running:
- A11r1's cold leg;
- validation of my #9746 dispatch-model refactor;
- the #9746 policy-test bisect;
- #9784 4b2 (615ad85a).

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- Before re-blessing a golden, normalize the digests and IDs, then diff again. An adapter version bump changes many public IDs, so a golden can fail on dozens of lines without any behavior change. Once the identity tokens are replaced by placeholders, either the diff is empty, which proves a pure rotation, or the remaining lines are the real behavior changes.
- `rust_copy_absence_other_file_edit_invalidates_warm_answer` shows another cost of a precision loss. When both answers are `PartialDiscovery`, a test that proves invalidation by watching the answer change loses its power. It needs a different observable, such as recomputation counts, to keep testing the same property.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

Running:
- A11r1's cold leg on EC2, under supervision;
- #9550's three fixes and suite reruns (86cfc67c);
- #9784 4b3, the owed tests (b2bf82b0), alongside 4c, the warm hits (d3945f85), in separate worktrees;
